 114.06, 114.22], ["beds", 114.22, 114.64], ["instead", 114.64, 115.04], ["of", 115.04, 115.2], ["washing", 115.2, 115.56], ["around", 115.56, 115.9], ["them,", 115.9, 116.26], ["up", 116.46, 116.6], ["to", 116.6, 116.78], ["65", 116.78, 117.3], ["%", 117.3, 117.76], ["off", 117.76, 118.18], ["right", 118.18, 118.52], ["now.", 118.52, 118.88], ["With", 119.16, 119.34], ["a", 119.34, 119.46], ["90", 119.46, 119.76], ["day", 119.76, 120.04], ["money", 120.04, 120.36], ["back", 120.36, 120.68], ["guarantee,", 120.68, 121.18], ["tap", 121.56, 121.74], ["below.", 121.74, 122.18]], "segments": [[0.0, 4.66, "Here's what happens to your airways. If you slide two capture cards under your mattress"], [4.66, 9.6, "and pillow and leave them there for four weeks, slide them in. That's the whole job."], [9.9, 14.32, "The first night while you sleep, the lure starts drawing dust mites up out of the foam,"], [14.64, 19.4, "the ones building up two inches under your face. That's the plant-derived pheromone lure,"], [19.62, 22.72, "pulling them away from the place you breathe for eight hours a night."], [22.96, 26.98, "By the end of week one, most people find they're not reaching for a tissue the"], [26.98, 32.62, "second they sit up. That's because every mite the lure pulls out stops dropping its 20 pellets"], [32.62, 37.52, "a day of Derpy One where your face sleeps, the allergen that breaks down the junctions"], [37.52, 42.28, "holding your airway lining together. Week two, you stop wondering if you're coming down with"], [42.28, 46.96, "something and that clearer by lunch feeling starts showing up at breakfast. That's the"], [46.96, 52.52, "adhesive, locking every mite the lure pulls in so what it catches comes out of your bed"], [52.52, 58.02, "instead of back into it. The craziest part? You haven't sprayed a thing. You haven't stripped the"], [58.02, 63.76, "bed. You haven't bought a new mattress but every single night the mattress you sleep on is giving"], [63.76, 69.36, "them up. Week four, by now most people are sleeping through more and waking up less blocked."], [69.64, 74.62, "Mornings start the way they did years ago and that background dread before you even open your"], [74.62, 80.04, "eyes is finally gone for you and for whoever shares your bed. How is this possible?"], [80.04, 84.64, "Most mite products try to kill them but every dead one stays in the bed,"], [84.84, 91.1, "carrying the same allergen as a live one. This one pulls them out alive. Dust mites have no eyes."], [91.34, 96.66, "They find each other by scent, a chemical signal. Capture cards mimic that signal. Drawing them"], [96.66, 102.4, "up out of the foam and the adhesive locks them on. It's lure and trap the way pest control"], [102.4, 107.98, "has caught things for decades aimed at the one place nobody had. The inside of a mattress"], [107.98, 113.76, "because a dead mite can't walk to a card. Over 30,000 homes are already pulling them"], [113.76, 120.04, "out of their beds instead of washing around them, up to 65% off right now. With a 90 day"], [120.04, 122.18, "money back guarantee, tap below."]]}